{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Hecke.RowCap","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Hecke.RowCap","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Choose.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.Card","lean:module:Mathlib.Logic.IsEmpty","lean:module:Mathlib.Order.Fin.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.RowCap.alt_channel_empty_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.RowCap.alt_channel_empty_iff","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/RowCap.lean#L158-L161","doc":"Reproves `weyl_dim_alt_eq_zero_iff` through the general cap: the singlet is\nempty exactly below three colours. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.RowCap.choose_eq_zero_iff_isEmpty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.RowCap.choose_eq_zero_iff_isEmpty","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/RowCap.lean#L151-L156","doc":"The `n = 3` singlet channel `dim V_{(1³)} = C(N,3)` vanishes exactly when\nthe column of three boxes cannot be filled. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.RowCap.staircase_two_nonempty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.RowCap.staircase_two_nonempty","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/RowCap.lean#L139-L142","doc":"Only `ρ₂ = (2,1)` among the staircases survives at `N = 2`, and it is the\ncase the conjecture block itself calls untestable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.RowCap.staircase_four_isEmpty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.RowCap.staircase_four_isEmpty","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/RowCap.lean#L135-L137","doc":"`(4,3,2,1)` — the staircase `ρ₄`, four rows — likewise. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.RowCap.staircase_three_isEmpty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.RowCap.staircase_three_isEmpty","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/RowCap.lean#L130-L133","doc":"`(3,2,1)` — the staircase `ρ₃`, three rows — carries no states at `N = 2`.\nThis is the block the staircase electroweak residual reads `cot θ_W` off. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.RowCap.isEmpty_of_three_rows","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.RowCap.isEmpty_of_three_rows","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/RowCap.lean#L123-L128","doc":"**At the framework's fibre, every partition with three or more rows is\nempty.**  This is the general form of what the corpus measured blockwise: the\n`ℓ(λ) > 2` sector spans the kernel of `H_n(q) → TL_n(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.RowCap.fibreDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.RowCap.fibreDim","kind":"def","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/RowCap.lean#L119-L121","doc":"The framework's fibre dimension. `abbrev` rather than `def` so that\n`omega` sees through it in the corollaries below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.RowCap.nonempty_columnFilling_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.RowCap.nonempty_columnFilling_iff","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/RowCap.lean#L107-L112","doc":"The cap as a biconditional: a column of `r` boxes is fillable from `N`\ncolours exactly when `r ≤ N`.  The forward direction is the pigeonhole above;\nthe reverse exhibits `Fin.castLE` as a witness. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.RowCap.forces_N_ge_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.RowCap.forces_N_ge_length","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/RowCap.lean#L102-L105","doc":"`N_min(λ) = ℓ(λ)`, in the direction that matters: a nonempty channel forces\nthe fibre to be at least as large as the partition is tall. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.RowCap.isEmpty_columnFilling_of_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.RowCap.isEmpty_columnFilling_of_lt","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/RowCap.lean#L96-L100","doc":"**The row cap.**  A column longer than the number of colours cannot be\nfilled.  With `r = ℓ(λ)` this is `SSYT(λ, N) = ∅` whenever `ℓ(λ) > N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.RowCap.le_of_columnFilling","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.RowCap.le_of_columnFilling","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/RowCap.lean#L89-L94","doc":"**A column of `r` boxes needs at least `r` colours.**\n\nThe pigeonhole step, and the only mathematical content in the file: a strictly\nincreasing map is injective, and an injection `Fin r → Fin N` forces `r ≤ N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.RowCap.columnFilling_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.RowCap.columnFilling_injective","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/RowCap.lean#L82-L85","doc":"A column filling is injective — the content of \"strictly increasing\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.RowCap.ColumnFilling","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.RowCap.ColumnFilling","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/RowCap.lean#L77-L80","doc":"A strictly increasing filling of a column of `r` boxes by colours in\n`Fin N`.  This is the restriction to the first column of a semistandard Young\ntableau of shape `λ` with entries in `{1, …, N}`, where `r = ℓ(λ)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}